WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:03.810
Spring cleaning has
taken a whole new meaning

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:06.330
as millions of people
stay in to curb the spread

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:09.220
of the coronavirus and
realize just how dirty

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:11.150
everything in their home is.

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:12.950
But with so much
misinformation floating around

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:15.970
about what works and what
doesn't, what can you do?

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:18.800
I got a little help over
Skype from Mikhail Varshavski,

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.890
better known as Doctor
Mike, to get the facts

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:23.000
about how to keep our stuff clean.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:23.833
- Well, the first thing you need

00:00:23.833 --> 00:00:26.590
to do is when you walk
inside from the outdoors,

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:28.280
you need to disinfect your body.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.890
It doesn't mean taking a full shower,

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:32.240
it means washing your
hands very thoroughly,

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.710
taking your shoes off,
leaving them by the door,

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:36.630
because that's the easiest way to bring in

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:38.360
those germs from the outside in.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:39.560
We don't want that to happen.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:40.393
How do we fight it?

00:00:40.393 --> 00:00:42.920
Washing our hands. And then the thing

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:44.140
that our hands touch most,

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:47.610
especially nowadays, are our cellphones.

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.350
So we need to disinfect these bad boys

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:51.200
when we come from the outdoors as well.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.920
Because we wash our hands, but
we were just touching this,

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.610
so all the viruses, all the bacteria,

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:57.320
is still alive on the cellphone.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:00.270
In fact, Apple just put out a
great release on how to clean

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:03.620
your cellphones properly
so you don't damage them.

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:06.540
- Looking at Apple's guidelines
for how to clean my iPhone,

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.150
I'm 100% okay doing
what I have been doing,

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.650
but probably should be doing more often,

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:12.940
which is using a wipe

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:17.700
and just gently wiping
the exterior surfaces.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.750
Now I just need to know which
of these cleaning products

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:22.270
to actually use on other
things around the house.

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:25.350
- If you're going to be using
any kind of bleach product,

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:28.420
it is recommended that you do
it in an open-air environment.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:29.930
So either you open up a window

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:31.970
or you do it in a well ventilated room,

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:35.790
because the bleach can aerosolize
and irritate your eyes.

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:38.720
There are products that can
disinfect without bleach.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:40.970
That being said, there
is no miracle product

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:42.170
that's better than the other.

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:43.760
Ready the labels very carefully.

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:46.520
They'll tell you which one is
a truly disinfecting product.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:49.181
In fact, if you look on some
of the products you'll see

00:01:49.181 --> 00:01:53.250
that coronavirus is on the list of things

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:55.050
that these disinfectants treat

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:57.920
because this novel coronavirus is not

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:00.320
the first coronavirus we've seen.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.070
Coronavirus is simply a strain of viruses

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:05.830
that cause all sorts of
respiratory conditions.

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:07.330
I've never noticed this
on products before,

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:09.340
so I went looking at some
of the disinfecting products

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:11.000
that I have around my house.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.637
And these handy wipes explicitly say

00:02:12.637 --> 00:02:14.870
"the human coronavirus."

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:16.390
I've also been using these wipes on a lot

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:19.330
of other surfaces around
my house like doorknobs,

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:23.520
light switches, faucets, remote controls.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:25.500
- There's been a couple
of research articles

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.071
that came out testing how
long this virus survives

00:02:28.071 --> 00:02:30.150
in different temperatures, humidities,

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.920
on different surfaces, even in the air.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:34.990
And copper seems to be
one of those surfaces

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:37.580
that the virus lives a very
short amount of time on

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.300
when you compare it to
something like plastic or steel.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:41.630
Why is that problematic?

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:43.560
Well, the majority of
our household products,

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:46.230
our mice, our keyboards,
they're made of plastic.

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:48.260
So it's easy, that if
your hands are dirty,

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:51.610
to have it live for a long
period of time on these products.

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:53.710
- So my wipes are going
to be a permanent addition

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:55.630
to my work-from-home setup.

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:58.640
Also because my coworkers
like to walk on my keyboard

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:01.730
and interact with me at my
dining table-slash-desk.

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:03.550
At least I don't have to worry
about taking these two out

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:06.160
for a walk and bringing
the coronavirus back in.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:09.080
- There's been a lot of talk
about pets being carriers

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:11.240
of this virus, and while
we haven't seen evidence

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:13.250
of them truly being sickened by this virus

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:14.840
and then getting their owners sick,

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:18.870
what we have seen is pets acting
like a surface contaminant.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:21.890
So if your walking outside and
someone asks to pet your dog,

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:25.610
respectfully ask them to
practice proper social distancing

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:28.570
so that they don't leave the
virus on your dog's hair,

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:30.260
so that when you come
in and start petting it

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:32.030
now the virus is on your hands.

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:33.540
That's a strong recommendation.

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:35.550
Also, very simple, when you're coming

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:38.550
in from the outdoors, wipe
your dogs' or cats' paws

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:40.627
so that they don't
bring the virus indoors.

00:03:40.627 --> 00:03:43.887
The virus does live a much
shorter time on surfaces

00:03:43.887 --> 00:03:46.640
in the environment where there's sun

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:49.690
because the sun is natures
disinfectant with its UV rays.

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:51.529
But that being said,
there's still a possibility

00:03:51.529 --> 00:03:53.300
that someone could have sneezed,

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.260
your dog or cat could have stepped on that

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:56.780
and then bring it inside the house.

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:58.780
So practice proper social distancing.

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:00.960
Clean them just like
you're cleaning yourself,

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:03.460
and you'll be able to be safe.

